    "title": "Evolutionary Resilience and Strategies for Climate Adaptation",
    "summary": "This article develops a four-dimensional framework for resilience—incorporating persistence, adaptability, transformability, and preparedness—to critically evaluate London's draft climate change adaptation strategy. The authors argue that the strategy relies too heavily on a rigid, engineering-based model of resilience focused on bouncing back to a previous state, rather than embracing an evolutionary approach that fosters transformation and social learning.",
